A feed sets the watchdog's deadline and leaves the core's timer as it was,
so a core that idles sleeps past the deadline it was fed for;
the core that fed the watchdog wakes for its deadline.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: the watchdog comes due before the timer wakes for it

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -60,7 +60,6 @@ void irq_set_bits(struct irq *irq, uint32_t bits)
 void sched_watchdog(uint32_t deadline)
 {
     watchdog = (struct watchdog){ .armed = true, .core = (uint8_t)core_index(), .deadline = deadline };
-    wake_for(deadline);
 }
 
